<title>USA: Ivex Packaging buys polystyrene operation.</title>
<headline>Ivex Packaging buys polystyrene operation.</headline>
<dateline>LINCOLNSHIRE, Ill. 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ivex Packaging Corp said Monday it acquired the oriented polystyrene business of Viskase Limited, a British subsidiary of Envirodyne Industries Inc.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not announced.</p>
<p>Ivex said the operation is the largest extruder of oriented polystyrene in Europe. The business generated revenues of about $20 million in 1996, Ivex said.</p>
<p>Ivex is a specialty packaging company that makes plastic and paper products for the consumer, medical, industrial and electronic markets.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
